Mesa 26.3.0 over 26.3.0-rc3 (nvk/MESA_BASE, 90a959eb), for the 13 files of that range that the NVK build reads.
Upstream text (MIT licence), unchanged: `git diff mesa-26.3.0-rc3 mesa-26.3.0` (tag commit 0a6fa60a) for these files.
Only the line numbers of the hunk in sm120_instr_latencies.rs differ, because the chain adds three lines above it.
The commits of the 26.3 branch in that range that touch these files, oldest first; in brackets the Mesa main commit
each was cherry-picked from:
  commit 1cff8320 (main 1d6fe659) compiler/nir: add missing intrinsic to avoid hitting assert
  commit 87772f33 (main e7e773e9) util/vl_vlc: allow removebits at the top of the bit buffer
  commit 4697a1d2 (main 1c3e49ad) util/rbsp: check each byte once for emulation prevention
  commit 2351a39d (main 801952de) nak: Fix missing scoreboard for uniform Ldcg on SM120
  commit b20a3da9 (main 4927b35f) nir: don't hardcode dedup_entry size in static_assert
  commit 4b42d801 (main 607364a0) nir: allow nir_cmat_tensor_load to be smaller than its const_index slots
  commit 17ee1c0e (main 00a0489f) nir/lower_goto_ifs: Sort sets in debug prints
  commit 9b1ea04a (main d65e16af) nir/lower_goto_ifs: Add some additional validation
  commit 69bfc55f (main 06bddf8a) util/set: Make some parameters const
  commit d9989e0c (main 170450f1) util/set: Add a couple set union helpers
  commit 1796dfc7 (main 0599e007) nir/lower_goto_ifs: Use the new set helpers
  commit 7d95cdd3 (main 60bdade9) nir/lower_goto_ifs: Expand/reformat some of the debug prints
  commit d75b0ba4 (main 0abe1db7) nir/lower_goto_ifs: Track outside blocks separately from break
  commit 2fdf24ad (main 77a21c6c) util: Add more ways to delete from dynarray
  commit b0281215 (main 880e93b6) nir: fix RANGE handling for load_ubo in lower_mem_access_bit_sizes
  commit 95a24bda (main 9703ac81) nir/opt_access: do not infer ACCESS_CAN_REORDER with shader interlock
  commit def7ef59 (main 88068706) nir/lower_multiview: Check variable modes before deleting
For an RTX 50 the one that matters is the Ldcg commit: the result of a uniform Ldcg (a load through the constant cache)
had no scoreboard on SM120, so an instruction could read the register before the load had finished.
Left out of the range on purpose: VERSION and the meson >= 1.5.0 requirement (the base stays rc3; the GCC-only qsort_r
check in the same file goes with them) and every file this build does not compile (GLSL, X11 WSI, other drivers).

